    "definition": "Minimize comparator count of an ascending sorting network; retain17 wires, add18 and19. Depth is reported separately and is not the objective.",
    "primary_source": "Sol read Dobbelaere SorterHunter table at https://bertdobbelaere.github.io/sorting_networks.html. Live size intervals are68–77 for18 and73–85 for19; lowest listed depth is a separate field. Exact77/85 comparator lists archived from pinned author revision8ba90df607cbdc339409e0b173b5a2ffd60fc911. AI-use status is not disclosed.",
    "human_method": "Reconstruct Batcher odd-even merge with sentinel wires trimmed from32 to n. With +infinity on high padding wires and min-to-low comparators, padding never enters real wire positions. Traditional90/98 comparator baselines reproduced and verified.",
    "independent_method": "Sol personally ran human and reference. In contrast to the checker bitset per wire, the audit packs each binary input as its own uint32 and uses conditional swaps, then checks the exact sorted popcount pattern for all262144 and524288 inputs. Feasible public scores77/85 match. No known size optimality proof found in checked sources.",
    "admission": "All five strict programs and complete declared-score, malformed, cold export, error/nonfinite/timeout and replay controls passed. The task agent restored immutable input-pattern caching before final replay to fit default search budget, without reducing binary cases. Original17-wire archives retained."
